  <programlisting><string>* in this case the mantissa is shifted right by one or two bits</string><string>
</string></programlisting>
  <para unique="1046232">
   <string>A numerically exact implementation of VRCP14xx can be found at </string><anchor id="message URL https://software.intel.com/en-us/articles/reference-implementations-for-IA-approximation-instructions-vrcp14-vrsqrt14-vrcp28-vrsqrt28-vexp2"/><underline><string>https://software.intel.com/en-us/articles/refer&#173;ence-implementations-for-IA-approximation-instructions-vrcp14-vrsqrt14-vrcp28-vrsqrt28-vexp2</string></underline><string>.</string></para>
  </longdesc>
 <subsection title="Intel C/C++ Compiler Intrinsic Equivalent">
  <para unique="1046254">
   <string>VRCP14PD __m512d _mm512_rcp14_pd( __m512d a);</string></para>
  <para unique="1046255">
   <string>VRCP14PD __m512d _mm512_mask_rcp14_pd(__m512d s, __mmask8 k, __m512d a);</string></para>
  <para unique="1046256">
   <string>VRCP14PD __m512d _mm512_maskz_rcp14_pd( __mmask8 k, __m512d a);</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="SIMD Floating-Point Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046258">
   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Other Exceptions">
  <para unique="1046263" format="xIndent1">
   <string>See </string><link linkend="79250: 06_Table: Table 2-49. Type E4 Class Exception Conditions"><string>Table&#160;2&#8209;51, &#8220;Type E4 Class Exception Conditions.&#8221;</string></link></para>
  </subsection>
 </instruction>
